WEBVTT

00:10.580 --> 00:14.210
It's finally done.
Our new house is complete.

00:14.460 --> 00:16.880
Looking at it now, it really is huge.

00:17.290 --> 00:19.210
Keep on digging!

00:19.540 --> 00:21.460
We're going to add a cellar

00:21.460 --> 00:23.040
You want me to keep going?

00:23.040 --> 00:25.290
We need big support beams, too!

00:25.630 --> 00:28.080
Here comes the swing. Fore!

00:28.250 --> 00:29.040
Yup.

00:29.420 --> 00:32.670
I had an inkling while working
that it would turn out like this, but still.

00:32.670 --> 00:35.420
And we helped out with the design.

00:35.540 --> 00:36.540
Right?

00:36.540 --> 00:37.460
Yup.

00:37.460 --> 00:39.130
We also made sure that
the requests of the future residents

00:39.130 --> 00:40.920
were all addressed during construction.

00:40.920 --> 00:43.380
I'm a resident too, you know.

00:43.670 --> 00:47.920
It wouldn't feel right if you didn't have
the nicest house here, Hiraku!

00:48.750 --> 00:50.540
Let's tour the interior.

00:54.630 --> 00:57.420
The structure inside looks a lot like
the house you live in, Lea.

00:57.540 --> 00:59.580
Right now we're in the main hall.

00:59.580 --> 01:02.380
We designed it so that everyone could
gather here and chat or hang out.

01:03.750 --> 01:06.750
And this here is your room, Hiraku.

01:09.000 --> 01:10.880
I like it.

01:11.630 --> 01:15.000
And opposite your room
across the main hall is...

01:15.290 --> 01:16.670
the dining room.

01:18.750 --> 01:21.130
There's a kitchen in the back.

01:21.630 --> 01:24.170
We even set up more stoves outside.

01:24.880 --> 01:27.580
So this is the cellar, huh?

01:28.130 --> 01:31.170
This will be great for storing
food and firewood.

01:34.330 --> 01:36.380
I was hoping for my own room!

01:36.380 --> 01:39.170
It was getting crowded with
all the people we have now.

01:39.420 --> 01:41.130
It looks like you guys
really like your rooms.

01:41.130 --> 01:42.130
Yeah!

01:42.460 --> 01:44.880
So what's this room over here?

01:45.790 --> 01:48.040
This one has a bolt lock for some reason.

01:49.250 --> 01:50.920
Why did they put one here?

01:56.290 --> 01:58.290
I'll pretend I didn't see that.

01:58.580 --> 02:02.000
It's really exciting to finally see
our new house like this.

02:02.000 --> 02:04.000
Ah, I love everything about it.

02:08.290 --> 02:12.210
Looking up at that tree from here
makes it feel like it's watching over us.

02:12.790 --> 02:15.210
Yeah, this is a really great house.

02:15.630 --> 02:17.170
Thank you very much.

02:17.880 --> 02:21.250
After you've spent the winter here, if you
feel any part of the house is unsatisfactory

02:21.250 --> 02:23.290
please let me know so that we may fix it.

02:23.290 --> 02:24.330
Got it.

02:24.750 --> 02:26.790
There we go.

02:29.750 --> 02:33.420
In addition to my God statue, I decided
to make some statues of my dogs.

02:34.080 --> 02:36.540
I put them in front of the entrance
to the new house.

02:37.250 --> 02:39.790
Yeah, this is shaping up pretty nicely.

02:53.790 --> 02:55.790
<b>Farming Life in Another World</b>

02:55.580 --> 03:03.170
When you open your eyes and see
that pure white light, the story begins

03:03.170 --> 03:09.920
Stepping forth into a new world,
what kind of flowers will we make bloom?

03:10.130 --> 03:17.500
Even if it's cloudy,
even if we get dirty from a puddle

03:17.500 --> 03:20.330
We continue on

03:20.330 --> 03:27.080
There's a future we can't imagine
waiting for us, I'm sure of it

03:27.380 --> 03:30.960
Meeting, meeting, and connecting

03:30.960 --> 03:34.250
If you smile,
everyone around you will smile too

03:34.250 --> 03:38.290
Let's plant a small seed and nurture it

03:38.290 --> 03:42.380
One day it'll become a large flower

03:42.380 --> 03:45.880
Turn regrets and failures into fuel

03:45.880 --> 03:49.210
So that you're overflowing with colorful happiness

03:49.210 --> 03:53.420
We'll join hands and share

03:53.420 --> 03:59.250
Spread across the world, Flower Ring

04:15.880 --> 04:16.880
Hm.

04:17.130 --> 04:19.580
This looks like all the main ingredients.

04:20.000 --> 04:23.630
Ah, I overdid it out there
and now I'm starving.

04:23.630 --> 04:25.710
What are we eating today?

04:25.920 --> 04:29.290
I going to try and see if I can manage to make
a new dish we haven't tried yet.

04:29.290 --> 04:31.250
Something new?

04:31.250 --> 04:32.290
Yeah.

04:32.290 --> 04:33.750
It's called curry.

04:34.080 --> 04:36.670
Huh, I've never heard of that.

04:36.670 --> 04:39.080
You're going to try to make it?

04:39.080 --> 04:42.210
Does that mean that this curry is
a difficult dish to make?

04:42.210 --> 04:46.170
Well, it can be easy to make,
but mastering the dish takes a lot of work.

04:46.170 --> 04:50.290
Usually, you'd just add roux to the pot
and cook it like that.

04:50.750 --> 04:51.630
Lu?!

04:51.830 --> 04:54.080
So that's the kind of stuff you're into?!

04:54.080 --> 04:55.210
You savage!

04:55.210 --> 04:56.750
What are you talking about?

04:57.710 --> 04:58.790
Wow.

04:58.790 --> 05:01.750
I didn't realize that you'd planted
all these crop fields, too!

05:01.750 --> 05:03.540
Yeah, I've been working at it little by little.

05:03.830 --> 05:06.130
There are a lot of plants here I don't recognize.

05:06.540 --> 05:07.710
Yup.

05:07.710 --> 05:09.330
That's because there are a lot of plants here

05:09.330 --> 05:11.170
that normally can't grow in climates
with any snowfall.

05:11.170 --> 05:12.790
With the almighty farming tool,

05:12.790 --> 05:16.500
I can grow plants that are
really sensitive to seasonal weather.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.130
The almighty farming tool really does it all.

05:20.380 --> 05:24.040
Okay, lets harvest the spices
we're going to need for the curry.

05:24.880 --> 05:26.500
First up is cumin.

05:26.500 --> 05:28.750
That's a cute sounding name.

05:28.750 --> 05:30.460
It looks like it's already dried out.

05:30.460 --> 05:34.670
<b>Cumin</b>

05:30.880 --> 05:32.460
After the flower has already bloomed,

05:32.460 --> 05:34.670
the seed that gets left behind
makes for a good spice.

05:35.000 --> 05:36.920
It's the spice that's most responsible
for curry's aroma.

05:39.330 --> 05:41.750
What a peculiar smell.

05:41.960 --> 05:46.170
<b>Turmeric</b>

05:42.170 --> 05:43.790
Next up is turmeric.

05:44.170 --> 05:46.170
It's the main ingredient
that gives curry its color.

05:46.380 --> 05:48.080
The part we care about is the root,

05:48.080 --> 05:50.460
but the part that grows
above ground is pretty huge.

05:50.460 --> 05:52.710
We dry out the part that grows
underground and use that.

05:53.080 --> 05:56.670
I ended up asking the girls
to dry them out for me.
Dry out, dry out. Become dry.<b></b>

05:56.670 --> 05:57.330
Dry out, dry out. Become dry.

05:57.330 --> 05:59.460
Magic really is handy.
Dry out, dry out. Become dry.<b></b>

05:59.630 --> 06:01.830
<b>Coriander</b>

05:59.880 --> 06:01.500
And next is coriander.

06:01.960 --> 06:04.130
We grind the seeds up into powder
and use them.

06:06.080 --> 06:08.880
This one has a nice and fresh,
fruit-like aroma.

06:08.880 --> 06:09.790
Yeah.

06:10.290 --> 06:13.580
The green leaves up top are called cilantro.

06:12.540 --> 06:14.080
<b>Cilantro</b>

06:15.540 --> 06:17.460
These have a potent aroma.

06:20.540 --> 06:21.960
Do you want to eat this?

06:26.210 --> 06:28.380
Well, I guess we like different flavors.

06:29.460 --> 06:30.960
Did you see that?

06:30.960 --> 06:32.040
Yeah.

06:32.040 --> 06:34.880
That's a plant capable of
driving off inferno wolves.

06:34.880 --> 06:37.580
I think that one will be worth researching.

06:39.170 --> 06:40.540
Next, we have black pepper.

06:41.290 --> 06:42.790
And cayenne peppers.

06:43.500 --> 06:46.630
Great. These are all the spices I'll need.

06:47.080 --> 06:47.920
Wait.

06:47.920 --> 06:49.130
Hold on.

06:52.460 --> 06:54.670
I've heard that girls think guys who make
their own curry from scratch,

06:54.670 --> 06:56.670
starting with the spices,
are a pain in the ass.

06:56.670 --> 06:58.790
I wonder if that's really true.

07:03.080 --> 07:04.040
Alright.

07:04.250 --> 07:06.130
This feels pretty authentic.

07:07.580 --> 07:08.670
By the way...

07:10.630 --> 07:12.420
are you my only helper, Lea?

07:12.420 --> 07:16.290
Yes. Lu and Tia said
they're busy with research.

07:16.500 --> 07:19.830
They said something about an
all powerful magical protection talisman.

07:20.960 --> 07:22.290
Whatever.

07:22.290 --> 07:23.420
We can handle it together.

07:23.420 --> 07:24.420
Yes!

07:26.960 --> 07:30.790
First, we start by heating up
the rapeseed oil we extracted.

07:32.210 --> 07:34.540
Then we add in the rabbit meat.

07:34.540 --> 07:35.460
Okay.

07:37.170 --> 07:38.460
While that's cooking,

07:38.460 --> 07:41.290
we grind up all the spices
except for the cumin into a powder.

07:41.880 --> 07:44.580
Is this enough for the meat?

07:44.920 --> 07:46.040
Yeah, looks like it.

07:46.040 --> 07:50.330
Once you've got some color on the meat,
take it off the heat so it doesn't overcook.

07:50.960 --> 07:53.880
Cook the cumin in the leftover bits
and juices from the meat

07:53.880 --> 07:55.500
to bring out the flavor and aroma.

07:55.920 --> 07:57.630
Be careful not to burn them.

07:58.380 --> 08:01.040
It's already starting to smell
like curry at this point.

08:01.040 --> 08:03.580
Wow. I've never smelled
anything like this before.

08:03.880 --> 08:10.170
Next, we need to focus on sautéing
the finely diced onions, ginger, and garlic.

08:10.710 --> 08:12.580
Sauté them without burning them.

08:13.420 --> 08:17.830
Now we add the diced tomatoes,
and we keep on sautéing everything.

08:20.250 --> 08:21.750
Would you like me to take over for a bit?

08:21.750 --> 08:23.080
Yeah, thanks.

08:23.670 --> 08:25.790
Once it's turned into a nice paste,
we can move on.

08:26.250 --> 08:28.960
Spices in. Boom! And we add salt, too.

08:30.210 --> 08:31.960
Cook it a little more.

08:31.960 --> 08:34.960
Then we add in the meat and
boiled soybeans along with some water.

08:34.960 --> 08:36.960
It already looks and smells delicious...

08:37.210 --> 08:40.130
Now we let it simmer
until the meat gets soft.

08:42.670 --> 08:44.500
Do we just need to wait for it now?

08:44.880 --> 08:47.170
Yeah, that's right...

08:47.170 --> 08:49.670
I feel like I'm forgetting something.

08:49.960 --> 08:51.130
What is it?

08:53.500 --> 08:54.540
It's naan!

08:54.540 --> 08:55.540
What's naan?!

08:55.540 --> 08:56.830
It's naan! Naan!

08:56.830 --> 08:58.130
It's naan? Naan?!

08:58.540 --> 09:01.080
I was so focused on the curry
that I forgot about it completely.

09:01.540 --> 09:03.170
Should I just make rice?

09:03.170 --> 09:06.000
No! I want naan with this curry.

09:06.290 --> 09:08.210
How many portions do I need to make?

09:08.210 --> 09:10.580
Me, Lu, Tia...

09:10.880 --> 09:12.420
And if I add in the elves, that makes...

09:12.790 --> 09:14.380
Well, it makes a lot.

09:15.080 --> 09:17.670
It's the same recipe as making regular bread
right up through the part where we let it rise.

09:17.670 --> 09:21.210
The difference is that now we
roll the dough out with a rolling pin.

09:21.210 --> 09:22.210
Okay.

09:24.670 --> 09:26.670
We're going to cook it now, right?

09:26.670 --> 09:28.130
That's right.

09:29.210 --> 09:31.500
You're supposed to cook it
inside of the stove,

09:31.500 --> 09:35.080
but I've seen people cook it using the
outside of a pot before, so we'll try that.

09:36.040 --> 09:39.170
What an interesting plant
this turned out to be.

09:39.170 --> 09:41.500
It doesn't appear to have been poisonous.

09:42.500 --> 09:44.420
What's going on there?

09:44.420 --> 09:47.460
I can smell something appetizing
coming from over there...

09:49.380 --> 09:51.500
And we haven't eaten yet.

09:51.500 --> 09:53.330
Yeah, you're right.

09:55.130 --> 09:57.000
Here's the last one.

09:57.460 --> 09:58.630
Alright.

09:59.710 --> 10:01.880
This should be just about done now.

10:07.830 --> 10:08.960
So this is...

10:09.210 --> 10:10.920
Curry, you said?

10:10.920 --> 10:13.250
It's got a... strange color to it.

10:13.830 --> 10:16.880
I'll need to work up a little courage
to try eating it.

10:16.880 --> 10:18.830
You don't need to be so shy.

10:19.580 --> 10:21.960
I think it probably came out pretty well.

10:22.830 --> 10:24.880
You scoop up the curry with the naan.

10:25.330 --> 10:27.420
That's why we made them flat like this.

10:30.250 --> 10:31.920
Yeah, it's great!

10:31.920 --> 10:33.540
This is real curry.

10:33.920 --> 10:36.330
I can smell all the spices in it.

10:43.380 --> 10:47.670
Oh my. This tingly spiciness
seems like it could become addicting.

10:48.080 --> 10:51.460
The ratio of the spices you use
changes the flavor, right?

10:51.460 --> 10:53.960
This will definitely be worth researching!

10:54.170 --> 10:57.500
Every bite I take makes me
want to eat even more of it!

10:58.170 --> 11:00.790
I'm glad to hear that you all like it.

11:01.330 --> 11:03.830
Well it's got a pretty unique taste,

11:03.830 --> 11:07.040
so if don't really like it then
there's no need to force yourself to...

11:09.670 --> 11:13.630
Um... would you mind
leaving a little for me?

11:16.920 --> 11:18.710
It really works!

11:18.710 --> 11:21.130
Well, it is pretty spicy...

11:22.460 --> 11:24.960
I'm glad the customers liked it,
but now I'm sold out.

11:25.540 --> 11:27.210
This isn't the first time it's happened.

11:28.500 --> 11:30.500
Wow, I'm stuffed.

11:30.500 --> 11:32.750
I definitely want to eat that again sometime.

11:33.000 --> 11:35.330
I've pretty much memorized the recipe!

11:35.330 --> 11:37.960
Let's try changing up how much of
the spices we use next time.

11:38.750 --> 11:41.960
Well they all liked it,
so I guess that's what's important.

11:42.630 --> 11:47.040
But still, eating just a few bites of curry
really makes you hungry.

11:48.000 --> 11:49.210
Farming Life...

11:49.210 --> 11:50.250
in Another...

11:50.250 --> 11:51.290
World

11:55.290 --> 11:57.420
This year's winter started to draw near.

11:58.500 --> 12:02.040
Once the snow starts to fall, we'll spend
most of our days inside the house.

12:02.540 --> 12:05.790
We need to finish our winter preparations
before that happens.

12:07.250 --> 12:09.670
We should be alright with
this much firewood.

12:10.540 --> 12:12.880
Hey, Zabuton!

12:13.330 --> 12:14.920
I brought you something.

12:15.380 --> 12:19.250
When it gets cold outside, Zabuton goes
into hibernation at the top of the tree.

12:22.290 --> 12:23.580
There we go.

12:23.580 --> 12:26.420
I made sure to ask for extra blankets
for the winter ahead of time.

12:26.420 --> 12:28.710
Thanks, we really needed these!

12:32.170 --> 12:33.170
Hey.

12:34.040 --> 12:35.420
Good work.

12:35.420 --> 12:37.130
You too. Good work.

12:37.540 --> 12:39.500
Lea and the elves are going to
keep working on the forge

12:39.500 --> 12:42.040
and some other projects
through the winter.

12:49.000 --> 12:53.540
I'm having Lu and Tia
preserve some food for the winter.

12:53.540 --> 12:56.750
We season the meat,
then smoke it and dry it.

12:57.500 --> 13:00.630
Kuro and the dogs won't be able to
hunt very well during the winter

13:00.630 --> 13:02.080
once it starts to snow.

13:02.750 --> 13:04.960
That's why I want to stock up
on as much as possible.

13:07.670 --> 13:08.880
Hey! Give those back!

13:08.880 --> 13:10.710
Well, I think we'll be okay as far as meat goes.
Hey! Give those back!<b></b>

13:10.710 --> 13:11.750
Well, I think we'll be okay as far as meat goes.

13:12.250 --> 13:15.290
Right now I'm working on
a way to preserve vegetables.

13:15.580 --> 13:17.750
The vegetables go into the boxes on top.

13:19.040 --> 13:20.880
Then they're covered in a sheet.

13:20.880 --> 13:22.920
And then we cover them with snow.

13:23.500 --> 13:25.330
It's called snow storage.

13:24.130 --> 13:26.130
<b>Vegetables</b>

13:25.330 --> 13:27.080
The bottom boxes are left empty

13:26.130 --> 13:28.960
<b>Vegetables</b>

13:26.130 --> 13:28.960
<b>Empty</b>

13:27.080 --> 13:28.960
and collect water from any snow
that melts to keep the vegetables dry.

13:29.670 --> 13:31.830
I'll try it out as soon as it snows.

13:31.830 --> 13:33.540
Here I go!

13:34.170 --> 13:36.250
I'm going to burn you to ashes!

13:36.500 --> 13:38.380
You're not supposed to burn them.

13:38.380 --> 13:40.000
I'm just messing around.

13:40.000 --> 13:41.830
I wish I could use magic.

13:47.710 --> 13:49.580
Even though I knew there was
no chance it would actually work,

13:49.580 --> 13:51.290
watching them use magic every day

13:51.290 --> 13:54.630
made me feel like I needed to try it
for some reason. I wonder why.

14:01.500 --> 14:03.880
Ignition may be a low level spell,

14:04.250 --> 14:07.250
but you still can't use it
without studying magic.

14:07.500 --> 14:09.460
Yeah, I guess you're right.

14:10.080 --> 14:14.080
You all make it look so easy
that I thought just maybe I could do it.

14:14.080 --> 14:16.630
I tried copying it,
but naturally it didn't work.

14:17.880 --> 14:22.080
The golems Tia summons are considered
difficult to use even among other magic users.

14:22.080 --> 14:26.000
Then doesn't that mean she's pretty amazing
since she can summon a bunch of them at once?

14:26.000 --> 14:26.830
Well yeah, but...

14:26.830 --> 14:27.830
Good job!
Well yeah, but...<b></b>

14:27.830 --> 14:30.580
I can do a lot of stuff too, you know?

14:30.580 --> 14:32.080
Of course I know.

14:33.460 --> 14:35.920
But still, you guys are all really amazing.

14:35.920 --> 14:37.920
I'm glad to know that I can
rely on you all to help.

14:37.920 --> 14:41.540
All I've been doing is
some garden work and cooking.

14:42.170 --> 14:43.710
What are you talking about?

14:43.710 --> 14:45.580
You're the most amazing one here.

14:46.540 --> 14:47.540
I am?

14:48.040 --> 14:51.580
Living out here like this
for as long as you have...

14:51.580 --> 14:53.790
that's something not just anyone can do.

14:55.130 --> 14:56.630
If you say so.

14:56.830 --> 14:58.040
I do.

14:58.330 --> 15:01.040
No one's been able to do this up until now.

15:01.880 --> 15:04.710
It's just you. You're the only one.

15:05.460 --> 15:06.630
Really?

15:06.630 --> 15:07.670
Yup.

15:25.830 --> 15:27.670
And so, winter had arrived.

15:28.170 --> 15:30.170
The snow began piling up.

15:30.750 --> 15:32.170
I think that should do it.

15:33.880 --> 15:37.540
We were spending more time indoors,
so we needing things to do for fun.

15:38.540 --> 15:40.630
I started with a classic, reversi.

15:41.290 --> 15:45.290
I built a chess set and a mahjong set as well.

15:46.750 --> 15:47.920
Uh...

15:47.920 --> 15:49.460
Reversi?

15:49.460 --> 15:50.420
Yeah.

15:50.830 --> 15:53.170
You play the game with
black and white pieces.

15:53.170 --> 15:54.920
When you surround an opponent's piece
on two sides with your own pieces,

15:54.920 --> 15:56.330
you flip it to your color.

15:56.330 --> 15:58.250
The game ends when the board
completely fills up,

15:58.250 --> 16:00.460
and whichever player has
the most pieces wins.

16:00.460 --> 16:01.880
Those are the only rules.

16:02.080 --> 16:04.210
What a simple game.

16:04.210 --> 16:06.460
Is it really any fun to play?

16:06.460 --> 16:08.170
How shortsighted.

16:08.170 --> 16:09.830
It's the simple design

16:09.830 --> 16:12.420
that allows for complicated strategies
to be developed in this game.

16:12.670 --> 16:14.250
You're absolutely right.

16:14.250 --> 16:17.380
It's amazing that you realized that
just from hearing the rules.

16:17.580 --> 16:19.040
It was nothing.

16:19.460 --> 16:22.500
I challenge you to a game right now, Tia!

16:22.670 --> 16:24.500
As you wish.

16:24.500 --> 16:28.670
After all, you and I have entered a
temporary truce since we started living here.

16:28.670 --> 16:31.330
Indeed. It's time we settled the score.

16:31.330 --> 16:33.790
L-let's try to relax and have some fun.

16:34.130 --> 16:35.460
I'll be white.

16:35.460 --> 16:37.130
That means that Tia gets to move first.

16:37.130 --> 16:38.580
Then I'm black!

16:38.580 --> 16:39.750
Fine...

16:49.630 --> 16:52.080
This is definitely a win for
the white team...

16:54.750 --> 16:56.960
Oh no, my hand slipped!

16:56.960 --> 16:59.040
She's the type that likes to
hit the reset button.

16:59.330 --> 17:01.130
Sorry about that, Tia.

17:01.130 --> 17:03.630
Since we don't know exactly
where the pieces were,

17:03.630 --> 17:05.250
it looks like we'll need to start over.

17:06.790 --> 17:08.330
Wh-what?

17:17.580 --> 17:19.790
Pressing reset doesn't work against her.

17:20.580 --> 17:23.580
Don't you find it embarrassing
to use your magic like that?

17:23.580 --> 17:25.170
Not as embarrassing as

17:25.170 --> 17:27.500
flipping the board because you think
you're about to lose the game.

17:29.250 --> 17:30.880
You haven't learned your lesson, have you?

17:32.040 --> 17:33.420
We're playing best of three!

17:33.420 --> 17:35.920
Fine be me. I accept your challenge.

17:36.920 --> 17:38.460
It looks nice and peaceful over there.

17:44.750 --> 17:46.210
What? Here?

17:47.380 --> 17:48.670
You're right!

17:49.040 --> 17:50.670
You're amazing, Kuro!

17:50.920 --> 17:52.830
He understands the rules?!

17:56.960 --> 17:59.540
They're actually playing the game right.

18:00.330 --> 18:02.880
At a glance, this seems cute.

18:03.170 --> 18:06.290
But I can feel a terrifying energy
coming from them.

18:10.290 --> 18:12.790
I better not challenge
any of them to a game.

18:12.790 --> 18:14.960
Ah, is your game done?

18:15.250 --> 18:16.920
I'm sure I'm not going to lose
to any of the dogs!

18:16.920 --> 18:17.920
Uh, Lu...

18:17.920 --> 18:19.460
I don't think that's a good idea...

18:20.170 --> 18:22.130
Come on, let's play a round.

18:25.130 --> 18:26.960
As I expected, she didn't have the courage

18:26.960 --> 18:29.040
to press the reset button
while playing against Kuro.

18:34.750 --> 18:36.460
Let's see...

18:44.790 --> 18:48.210
Even Kuro shouldn't be able to fully
understand the game of mahjong yet.

18:48.210 --> 18:49.920
It's far too complicated.

18:49.920 --> 18:51.040
This one here?

18:52.790 --> 18:54.750
It might seem a little childish, but...

18:54.750 --> 18:56.830
I'm going to take revenge for Lu now.

18:58.170 --> 18:59.080
Riichi!

19:00.420 --> 19:02.830
Then I call tsumo! No wait, I mean ron!

19:03.170 --> 19:04.710
That's ron for me, too.

19:05.080 --> 19:06.210
At least I think so.

19:06.830 --> 19:08.130
Double ron?!

19:08.130 --> 19:10.040
Wait, the yasume should save...

19:11.130 --> 19:11.960
me!

19:11.960 --> 19:13.290
What?!

19:15.130 --> 19:18.540
I-it's the 13 orphans...

19:16.500 --> 19:24.580
<b>Kuro</b>

19:16.500 --> 19:24.580
<b>Lea</b>

19:16.500 --> 19:24.580
<b>Tia</b>

19:16.500 --> 19:24.580
<b>Hiraku</b>

19:18.540 --> 19:21.000
Hey, isn't this yakuman?

19:21.000 --> 19:24.290
It seemed complicated at first,
but the game is actually pretty simple.

19:24.790 --> 19:29.330
Let's see, Hiraku doesn't have
any points left, so Kuro wins the game!

19:29.630 --> 19:32.380
Kuro, you're number one.

19:42.710 --> 19:45.380
I figured that only playing board games
all day wouldn't be good for our health,

19:46.080 --> 19:47.960
so I built a mini bowling set, too.

19:48.170 --> 19:49.460
Good luck.

19:49.460 --> 19:52.000
I'm definitely not just mad
that I lost at mahjong.

20:03.210 --> 20:05.130
Eight pins. Not bad.

20:05.630 --> 20:09.460
The arsonist and the serial killer
are really hard to take down, aren't they?

20:09.460 --> 20:11.920
The scam artist up front is surprisingly tough, too.

20:11.920 --> 20:18.880
<b>Scam Artist</b>

20:11.920 --> 20:18.880
<b>Arsonist</b>

20:11.920 --> 20:18.880
<b>Serial Killer</b>

20:12.380 --> 20:16.630
These nasty sounding titles are ones
we've given to each of the pins here.

20:16.630 --> 20:18.880
They were just normal pins
I'd carved at first, but...

20:19.170 --> 20:20.670
Why do we want to knock them down?

20:20.670 --> 20:22.170
Lu hit me with that question,

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Arsonist</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Pirate</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Bandit</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Scam Artist</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Bandit</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Pirate</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Bandit</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Bandit</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Pirate</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.630
<b>Serial Killer</b>

20:22.180 --> 20:25.630
so I decided the best answer was
"To take out the bad guys."

20:30.460 --> 20:31.750
Got 'em!

20:31.750 --> 20:33.380
I'm up next.

20:33.960 --> 20:35.960
I don't know if it's because
they enjoyed the simplicity of it,

20:36.330 --> 20:36.960
You did it!

20:36.960 --> 20:37.790
but the bowling was a big hit with them.
You did it!<b></b>

20:37.790 --> 20:38.960
but the bowling was a big hit with them.

20:42.130 --> 20:46.670
And so, we spent our winter all together,
nice and cozy inside and playing games.

20:50.920 --> 20:53.500
Those days went by faster
than we thought they would.

21:04.960 --> 21:07.710
The snow melted, and spring came.

21:13.960 --> 21:15.580
What a nice morning.

21:16.130 --> 21:18.170
It's gotten nice and warm outside.

21:18.960 --> 21:20.250
Morning...

21:20.250 --> 21:21.500
Good morning.

21:24.080 --> 21:25.330
Good morning.

21:25.330 --> 21:27.210
What are we going to do today?

21:27.210 --> 21:28.750
Let's see...

21:29.130 --> 21:31.630
I want to finish planting the crops
as soon as we can.

21:32.460 --> 21:36.000
I think it's about time that Zabuton
woke up from her hibernation.

21:36.000 --> 21:38.250
We still have some potatoes left, right?

21:38.250 --> 21:40.250
Yes, I believe so.

21:45.250 --> 21:48.380
Based on the number of taps,
it should be coming from this direction.

21:49.000 --> 21:50.000
It's up there!

21:52.830 --> 21:55.000
Something big is headed here...

21:55.460 --> 21:58.170
Is that... a dragon?!

21:58.170 --> 22:00.250
No, it's a wyvern!

22:00.540 --> 22:01.960
It can't be...

22:30.210 --> 22:38.960
I can feel the soft seasonal winds,
gently on my fingertips

22:39.290 --> 22:47.880
Let's search for what we love
in the clouds floating in the sky

22:47.880 --> 22:52.670
Forget about the hands of the clock for now

22:52.670 --> 22:57.080
Try taking one deep breath

22:57.080 --> 23:06.710
The rainbow-colored scenery
will resonate with my heart

23:08.040 --> 23:13.040
I'm sure any wish I have will come true

23:13.040 --> 23:17.580
Because you're by my side

23:17.580 --> 23:22.170
You make every day feel like a dream

23:22.420 --> 23:26.960
At that warm and kind place

23:26.960 --> 23:34.130
Keep showing me your smiling face forever

23:46.040 --> 23:47.460
<b>Next Time</b>

23:47.460 --> 23:50.960
<b>Episode 6</b>

23:47.460 --> 23:50.960
<b>This Is a Village</b>

23:47.460 --> 23:50.960
<b>Next Time</b>
